                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This would likely be a neutral, leaning towards positive, review if it was possible.\n\nHere was my previous review:\n---------------------\nIf this game was Early Access, I could understand it's current state. But as a finished product this game is very rough. At the time of this review, many of the achievements are not working at all (kill mobs, kill bosses, etc.). There is no collision with walls, trees, etc. You literally clip under rocks and grass on the ground. You can walk outside the visual edge of the levels. There are no key bindings or lists of what controls do what (I had to ask on the discussion forums to find out how to dash).\n\nWith a lot more polish, this game could be worth buying. Right now there are way too many competitors that do a much better job of this style of game for the same price point to recommend buying Spell Cast, although I hope that changes in the future.\n------------------------\n\nThe developer was quick to respond to these issues and fixed them nearly overnight, which is awesome. However, these are major issues that should have been caught with even a few minutes of playtesting and never should have made it into a finished product in the first place.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1653948013,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1654111664,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 10,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6710116863250732,
